# Test: ze show host memory returns /proc/meminfo inventory JSON without a daemon
# VALIDATES: offline fallback -- `show host memory` runs the in-process
#            host.DetectMemory when no daemon is reachable, producing JSON
#            with the always-present total-bytes / available-bytes / ecc-present
#            fields sourced from /proc/meminfo (+ edac counters).
# PREVENTS: regressions where show host memory silently requires a daemon,
#           or where the memory JSON drops its canonical kebab-case fields.
# PLATFORM: host inventory reads /proc/meminfo; the darwin detector
# (memory_other.go) returns ErrUnsupported at build time so the underlying
# feature cannot succeed. Skip on darwin per rules/os-specific-tests.md.
option=skip-os:value=darwin
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp { }
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show host memory
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains="total-bytes"
expect=stdout:contains="available-bytes"
expect=stdout:contains="ecc-present"
